{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PAUSED (2026-07-24) — option (A) implemented but blocked by a deeper finding.\n\nWIP parked, unpushed, at commit 5bf846df9 on branch `5128-local-never-signs`\n(worktree /Users/joeoakhart/5128-local-never-signs). lint + typecheck green.\n\nWhat (A) delivered and works:\n- The never-sign guard, decided from the resolved gate HANDLE rather than `verdict[\"source\"]`\n  (which is stamped after the sign decision, so a verdict-based guard would be a silent no-op).\n- Suite default migrated local -> attested/`ref=HEAD` in `tests/conftest.py`. This works\n  offline and is fast; failures dropped from 30 (naive guard, local default) to 5.\n- Uncovered a latent test-infrastructure bug: `_commit()` ran `git commit --allow-empty` with\n  NO `git add`, so it advanced HEAD without ever recording content. Harmless while the gate\n  read the working tree; invisible-content once it reads a snapshot. Added `_commit_all()`.\n- `test_pass_verdict_carries_a_passing_signature` no longer reviews with `source=\"local\"`\n  (AC3 satisfied — it had encoded the bypass as expected behavior).\n- Three regression tests pinning the fixed contract: local PASS unsigned, local review leaves\n  the claim gate blocked, and no signed attestation may carry a null `verified_at_sha`.\n\nTWO BLOCKERS, both discovered during implementation:\n\n1. Scoped drift is structurally unreachable in attested mode -> filed as\n   72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6 (athletic-esthetical-polecat), now a `depends_on` of this ticket.\n   The claim gate re-hashes dependencies at the signature's own pinned SHA\n   (`manifest.py:190-225`), so the comparison is a tautology and drift can never fire. The\n   five remaining test failures are not test bugs — they are this defect becoming visible\n   once the suite stops running in local mode. Production has this weakness TODAY,\n   independent of my change; the local-source default was masking it.\n\n2. A CONFLICTING authority I did not have when classifying this ticket. `manifest.py:206-207`:\n\n       BACK-OUT: a plan-review signed in local mode (or pre-S4b) carries no\n       ``verified_at_sha``; both sides then resolve to the working tree exactly as before\n       this consolidation.\n\n   That assumes local-mode-signed plan reviews EXIST and are supported, contradicting ADR 0005\n   / `repo_snapshot.SOURCE_LOCAL` / the CLI help that this ticket's `defect` classification\n   rests on. It does not obviously overturn ADR 0005 (a comment is weaker than an ADR), but it\n   is evidence the behavior may have been deliberate for plan review, and it must be\n   reconciled before this lands.\n\nOrder-of-work consequence: the working tree is the only MUTABLE hash basis, so removing\nlocal-source signing removes the only basis the drift machinery can exercise. 72d9 should\ntherefore land FIRST — it redefines the drift comparison against the current gate ref, after\nwhich this fix costs nothing extra."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784945590673248001,"uuid":"7f7da301-d9b0-4c58-8181-9da8b5c2a60e"}